        "id": 236964,
        "name": "",
        "username": "fjur",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-04-18T22:27:43.111Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I’m with <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/powerhound_2000\">@Powerhound_2000</a> on this one. <span class=\"hashtag\">#3</span> seems correct to me.</p>\n<p>Reason being, the Rules have no official notion of “secondary” or “primary” effects. There’s just Actions that are part of Abilities. The Rules don’t know care about relative die sizes for various Actions, they’re all equally part of the Ability.</p>\n<p>Similarly, that Mode only stops Boosts, it doesn’t say that it prevents you from using other parts of Abilities that also happen to contain Boosts.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-04-18T22:27:43.111Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
